Subject: [PATCH] Present: the path decided before the first picture where GL cannot draw into Direct3D's textures (TODO 417)

A player's Intel N100 (UHD Graphics, driver 32.0.101.7088) crashed inside Intel's OpenGL driver (igxelpicd64.dll) a few
pictures after the start, right at "the DXGI swap chain cannot take GL's pictures here: GL's own swap from now on": 13 of 20
starts without the IOP's boot, 5 of 17 with it, 0 of 12 with PS2X_PRESENT=gl. On every Intel PC the GL/Direct3D interop
refuses the pictures' NT-handle textures (6e) and the legacy-handle retry is not made there (TODO 311), so the present thread
learnt it on its first pictures and the window went to GL's own swap live: the present thread's GL context (in the window's
share group) deleted and the flip-model swap chain released while the GS renderer's context and the native renderer were
already drawing. Now dxgi::open() makes the textures once (in the present thread's context, on the window's thread, before
the first picture and before any other GL context exists) and drops them again; where they cannot be made the swap chain is
dropped at once and the window has GL's own swap from the start. Where they can be made nothing changes (the present thread
makes them anew on its first picture, as before). The live switch stays for the other reasons (failed presents, the picture
check, stuck pictures before the first shown one), made safer: the present thread's context is left in place instead of
deleted under the other contexts, and the presenting device's state is cleared and flushed before the swap chain is
released (Direct3D 11 destroys it late otherwise). PS2X_PRESENT_PROBE=0: as before; =early: tried before the swap chain is
made (none made where they fail).

diff --git a/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/ps2_host_present_dxgi.cpp b/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/ps2_host_present_dxgi.cpp
index 8ff5d0e..1a5d7db 100644
--- a/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/ps2_host_present_dxgi.cpp
+++ b/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/ps2_host_present_dxgi.cpp
@@ -240,6 +240,27 @@ namespace ps2_host_present::dxgi
             return s >= window.first && s < window.first + window.second;
         }
 
+        // (TODO 417) Where GL cannot draw into Direct3D's textures (every Intel PC: its interop refuses the NT-handle ones,
+        // 6e, and the legacy-handle retry is not made there - TODO 311), the window used to learn it from the present thread
+        // on its first pictures and went to GL's own swap live, a few pictures in: the present thread's context (sharing the
+        // window's textures) deleted and the swap chain dropped while the GS renderer's and the native renderer's contexts
+        // (the same share group) were drawing. On a player's Intel N100 that crashed inside Intel's GL driver in 13 of 20
+        // starts (0 of 12 with PS2X_PRESENT=gl). Now the textures are tried once in open(), before the first picture and
+        // before any other GL context exists; where they cannot be made the window has GL's own swap from the start.
+        // PS2X_PRESENT_PROBE=0: as before (found on the first pictures, the switch live); =early: tried before the swap chain
+        // is made (none made where they fail - the default makes it and drops it, as the live switch did: TODO 311 measured
+        // the movies' holds gone on the ThinkPad with a swap chain made and dropped).
+        int probeMode()
+        {
+            static const int mode = []()
+            {
+                const char *env = std::getenv("PS2X_PRESENT_PROBE");
+                const std::string v = env ? env : "";
+                return v == "0" ? 0 : v == "early" ? 2 : 1;
+            }();
+            return mode;
+        }
+
         // (TODO 362) A present that failed: counted in a row; the first of each kind said, with its code.
         enum Failure
         {
@@ -999,6 +1020,21 @@ namespace ps2_host_present::dxgi
             wglMakeCurrent(windowDc, windowContext); // (the present thread's from now on)
             return g.interopDevice != nullptr;
         }
+
+        // (TODO 417) The pictures' textures made once at the window's size in the present thread's context (on the window's
+        // thread, before the first picture), then dropped again: the present thread makes them anew on its first picture,
+        // as before. False: GL cannot draw into them here.
+        bool probePictures()
+        {
+            const HDC windowDc = wglGetCurrentDC();
+            const HGLRC windowContext = wglGetCurrentContext();
+            if (!wglMakeCurrent(g.partDc, g.partContext))
+                return true; // (cannot tell here: the present thread finds out, as before)
+            const bool made = fit(g.width, g.height);
+            dropPictures();
+            wglMakeCurrent(windowDc, windowContext);
+            return made;
+        }
     }
 
     // (TODO 98) The fence shared by the two devices (State::shareFence). PS2X_PRESENT_FENCE=0: none, as before (an A/B).
@@ -1125,6 +1161,18 @@ namespace ps2_host_present::dxgi
             close();
             return false;
         }
+        RECT client{};
+        GetClientRect(g.window, &client);
+        g.width = client.right - client.left > 0 ? static_cast<int>(client.right - client.left) : 1;
+        g.height = client.bottom - client.top > 0 ? static_cast<int>(client.bottom - client.top) : 1;
+        // (TODO 417) PS2X_PRESENT_PROBE=early: the textures tried before the swap chain is made
+        if (probeMode() == 2 && !probePictures())
+        {
+            std::fprintf(stderr, "[present] GL cannot draw into Direct3D's textures here (tried before the first picture, no swap chain "
+                                 "made): GL's own swap from the start\n");
+            close();
+            return false;
+        }
         // Variable refresh in a window takes presents allowed to tear.
         IDXGIFactory5 *factory5 = nullptr;
         if (SUCCEEDED(g.factory->QueryInterface(__uuidof(IDXGIFactory5), reinterpret_cast<void **>(&factory5))))
@@ -1134,10 +1182,6 @@ namespace ps2_host_present::dxgi
             factory5->Release();
         }
         g.swapChainFlags = g.tearing ? DXGI_SWAP_CHAIN_FLAG_ALLOW_TEARING : 0u;
-        RECT client{};
-        GetClientRect(g.window, &client);
-        g.width = client.right - client.left > 0 ? static_cast<int>(client.right - client.left) : 1;
-        g.height = client.bottom - client.top > 0 ? static_cast<int>(client.bottom - client.top) : 1;
         DXGI_SWAP_CHAIN_DESC1 desc{};
         desc.Width = static_cast<UINT>(g.width);
         desc.Height = static_cast<UINT>(g.height);
@@ -1157,6 +1201,15 @@ namespace ps2_host_present::dxgi
             return false;
         }
         g.factory->MakeWindowAssociation(g.window, DXGI_MWA_NO_ALT_ENTER | DXGI_MWA_NO_WINDOW_CHANGES);
+        // (TODO 417) The textures tried before the first picture: where GL cannot draw into them the swap chain is dropped
+        // again at once, before any picture and any other GL context, and the window has GL's own swap from the start.
+        if (probeMode() == 1 && !probePictures())
+        {
+            std::fprintf(stderr, "[present] GL cannot draw into Direct3D's textures here (tried before the first picture): the swap "
+                                 "chain dropped, GL's own swap from the start\n");
+            close();
+            return false;
+        }
         g.stop = false;
         g.abandon = false;
         g.finished.store(false, std::memory_order_relaxed);
@@ -1307,6 +1360,10 @@ namespace ps2_host_present::dxgi
 
     void close()
     {
+        // (TODO 417) A switch from a running present thread (the live fallback): the GS renderer's and the native
+        // renderer's contexts share the window's textures with the present thread's - its context is not deleted under
+        // them (nor its hidden window): left as it is, unused. PS2X_PRESENT_PROBE=0: deleted, as before.
+        const bool live = probeMode() != 0; // also before the first picture: deleting it crashes Intel's driver
         if (g.thread.joinable())
         {
             {
@@ -1345,14 +1402,34 @@ namespace ps2_host_present::dxgi
             g.interopDevice = nullptr;
             g.source = 0u;
         }
-        if (g.partContext)
-            wglDeleteContext(g.partContext);
+        if (live)
+            std::fprintf(stderr, "[present] the present thread's GL context is left in place (deleting it crashes some drivers)\n");
+        else
+        {
+            if (g.partContext)
+                wglDeleteContext(g.partContext);
+            if (g.partWindow)
+                DestroyWindow(g.partWindow);
+        }
         g.partContext = nullptr;
-        if (g.partWindow)
-            DestroyWindow(g.partWindow);
         g.partWindow = nullptr;
         g.partDc = nullptr;
         release(g_check.staging);
+        // (TODO 417) Nothing of the presenting device's left bound or queued before the swap chain goes: Direct3D 11 destroys
+        // it late otherwise, and the window must not be presented to by GL while a flip-model swap chain still holds it.
+        if (probeMode() != 0)
+        {
+            if (g.context)
+            {
+                g.context->ClearState();
+                g.context->Flush();
+            }
+            if (g.shareContext)
+            {
+                g.shareContext->ClearState();
+                g.shareContext->Flush();
+            }
+        }
         release(g.swapChain);
         release(g.shareFence);
         release(g.presentFence);
